{"id":"alta-via-1","title":"Alta Via 1, Dolomites","who":"Classic route · the queen of Dolomite hut treks","when":"Late June to mid-September, when the rifugi are open","vehicle":"On foot, 8–11 days, mountain huts","kind":"walk","color":"#be185d","summary":"About 120 km south through the pale towers of the Dolomites from Lago di Braies to near Belluno: the Fanes plateau, First World War tunnels at Lagazuoi, the Cinque Torri, the Civetta's great wall, and nights in rifugi with polenta and grappa. No via ferrata needed, though some passages have cables.","sources":[{"label":"Tumbarumba: Alta Via 1, 2025 practical notes","url":"https://tumbarumba.co.uk/MOUNTAIN%20WALKING/ALTA%20VIA%201%20-%202025/The Practical.html"},{"label":"Fastest Known Time: Alta Via 1, August 2025","url":"https://fastestknowntime.com/fkt/matteo-grassi-alta-dolomiti-n-1-italy-2025-08-24"}],"approximate":"The usual huts; the line follows mountain paths where they were found.","km":96,"bbox":[12.0043,46.215,12.127,46.6952],"stops":[{"name":"Lago di Braies","place":"Lago di Braies","at":[46.6947,12.0858],"text":"The emerald lake at the start, crowded at noon, magical at dawn.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Pragser_Wildsee_Seekofel_von_Bucht.jpg/500px-Pragser_Wildsee_Seekofel_von_Bucht.jpg","page":"Pragser Wildsee","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pragser_Wildsee_Seekofel_von_Bucht.jpg","credit":"STirol","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Rifugio Sennes","place":"Rifugio Sennes","at":[46.6536,12.0594],"text":"Up past the Croda del Becco to the high Sennes plateau.","source":{"label":"Tumbarumba (2025)","url":"https://tumbarumba.co.uk/MOUNTAIN%20WALKING/ALTA%20VIA%201%20-%202025/The Practical.html"}},{"name":"Fanes","place":"Rifugio Lavarella","at":[46.6112,12.007],"text":"The Fanes alp, land of Ladin legends."},{"name":"Lagazuoi","place":"Rifugio Lagazuoi","at":[46.5278,12.0081],"text":"The highest hut at 2,752 m; down through the war tunnels next morning.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Lagazuoi_cable_car_2.jpg/500px-Lagazuoi_cable_car_2.jpg","page":"Lagazuoi","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lagazuoi_cable_car_2.jpg","credit":"kallerna","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Cinque Torri","place":"Rifugio Averau","at":[46.4996,12.0406],"text":"Five rock towers and open-air war trenches.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Cortina_%2850162425826%29.jpg/500px-Cortina_%2850162425826%29.jpg","page":"Cinque Torri","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cortina_%2850162425826%29.jpg","credit":"Luca Sartoni from Vienna, Austria","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Città di Fiume","place":"Rifugio Città di Fiume","at":[46.4369,12.1226],"text":"Under the \"throne of God\", Monte Pelmo.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Monte_Pelmo_2.jpg/500px-Monte_Pelmo_2.jpg","page":"Monte Pelmo","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monte_Pelmo_2.jpg","credit":"kallerna","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Civetta","place":"Rifugio Coldai","at":[46.4023,12.0755],"text":"Lago Coldai and the Civetta's 1,200 m north-west wall."},{"name":"Rifugio Carestiato","place":"Rifugio Carestiato","at":[46.3214,12.0705],"text":"Under the Moiazza towers."},{"name":"La Pissa (Belluno)","place":"La Pissa, Belluno","at":[46.2167,12.1],"text":"Down through the Schiara massif's foothills to the bus for Belluno.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Belluno_5042.jpg/500px-Belluno_5042.jpg","page":"Belluno","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belluno_5042.jpg","credit":"Ashley Pomeroy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"walk","km":9,"line":[[46.6952,12.0881],[46.688,12.0852],[46.678,12.0949],[46.6696,12.0942],[46.6592,12.0607],[46.6536,12.0596]]},{"by":"walk","km":10,"line":[[46.6536,12.0596],[46.6458,12.0603],[46.6403,12.0511],[